---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="resources — tiny soft computer"
  description="Bill of materials and classroom-friendly alternatives for the tiny soft computer kit."
  active="resources"
>

  <section class="hero" style="padding-top: 2.5rem;">
    <p class="kicker">resources</p>
    <h1>what's in the kit, and what you can swap</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      for educators adapting this kit to their own classroom, budget, or
      what's actually in stock.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>bill of materials</h2>
    <ul class="plain">
      <li>Adafruit RP2040 Feather ThinkInk</li>
      <li>2.13" 212×104 Flexible Monochrome eInk display (ILI0373)</li>
      <li>tactile push button</li>
      <li>2 wires (alligator clips or jumper wires)</li>
      <li>USB-C cable</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      exact current pricing changes, check Adafruit's site directly
      before ordering in bulk.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <h2>alternatives</h2>
    <p>
      the flexible eInk display has a real hardware limit: it can only
      redraw once every few minutes (see <a href="/about">about</a> for
      why). if that pacing doesn't fit your classroom's timing, a
      monochrome OLED display swaps in cleanly, same microcontroller,
      instant refresh, no waiting. it trades away the eInk's paper-like
      quality for speed.
    </p>
    <p class="note">
      full alternative wiring and code notes coming soon.
    </p>
  </section>

</Layout>
